        ],
        "notes": "Depth of the 2.7 µm absorption of OH in Mg-rich clays (phyllosilicates), from the archived Dawn VIR global mosaic (Survey phase, public V2 calibration). The color scale spans this map's own 2nd to 98th percentile, 0.229 to 0.283, with the rainbow core of the Frigeri et al. (2019), Figure 7 bar. The archived values are deeper than that paper's (median 0.255 against its peak near 0.20): the paper used an artifact correction and instrument response (Carrozzo et al. 2016) that were never released, and a different continuum. Scan stripes remain for the same reason. Gray grid: beyond 60° latitude and other unmeasured pixels.",
