        "notes": "Depth of the 3.1 µm absorption of ammonium (NH4) in clays, reduced here from Dawn VIR calibrated cubes with the continuum of Frigeri et al. (2019): column stripes and spikes removed, each cube brought to 30° phase, each pixel footprint mapped, overlaps averaged and seams blended as ISIS3 noseam does. Survey and HAMO cubes set every cell they saw; LAMO, then Approach cubes fill the rest. The color scale spans this map’s own 2nd to 98th percentile, 0.106 to 0.151, with the rainbow core of the Frigeri et al. (2019), Figure 7 bar. Values run deeper than the paper’s (median 0.121 against its peak near 0.09) because its response correction (Carrozzo et al. 2016) was never released; the pattern ranks close to its map (Spearman 0.89). Gray grid: beyond 60° latitude and the 1.3% no cube saw under 70° incidence and emission.",
